module gunbc.rung_drop_amendment.checker_edge_withheld_over_the_per_pr_runner_class

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.rung_drop_amendment { RungDropAmendment }

data checker_edge_withheld_over_the_per_pr_runner_class: RungDropAmendment = RungDropAmendment {
  drop_identity: "compiler_change_refusals_land_outside_every_compiled_closure" as NonEmptyStr,

  amended: "2026-09-30",

  later_event: "gunbc#12761 landed the edge this drop's loss is about: the checker is a dependency of every module it judges. v2.workflow.floor_subject_seed checker_subject_rule reads the running claim_executor's cargo dep-info (never a hand list; rustc's per-crate record is refused because it omits the infer crate) and the run's changed paths, and chooses EveryAdmittedModule when a changed path is a checker input. The specimen is gunbc#12441, which edited v1_compiler_infer.rs and whose landing run 36641740799 left out v2.test.claim.type_param_binder_frame, the module its new check refused. APPLYING the rule on a required run was then measured over the per-PR runner class. neat-boar-16 ran it on srv1 over main 0207c666 with gunbc#12765 (the prepare-closure-resolve fix): 7057 modules resolved, 2142 s wall, 43.66 GiB peak, against the 28 GiB class and the 30-minute line. The retained memory is the v1 strict typecheck (sleek-ibex-207 owns the cut). On the fleet, gunbc#12761's own required run 36751831054 (floor job 110012128298, head 5e9f495, main with gunbc#12765) prepared the same 7057 modules in about 51.7 minutes (17:40:07 to 18:31:50) at about 24.8 GiB, against about 2 minutes for an ordinary preparation (main run 36653654636). So the memory fits the per-PR class on that runner and the time does not. So the widening is WITHHELD under this drop by the declared standing v2.workflow.floor_subject_seed checker_widening_standing, and every required run that changes a checker input prints rule=EveryAdmittedModule applied=false withheld_under=gunbc.rung_drop.compiler_change_refusals_land_outside_every_compiled_closure. That same measurement refused on 34 blocking diagnostic lines (30 distinct sites) in 14 files, identical on srv1 and on the fleet,, all already on main, and those are this drop's standing population at that revision. It did not refuse on std.algebra's 86 GateAdvisoryTypecheck diagnostics, which are advisory by is_interpreter_blocking_diagnostic, the known-negative control.",

  bearing: "the edge is modeled, derived and decided on every run, and only its application is withheld. The drop's loss is unchanged: a checker change still lands with its new refusals unseen outside the narrow subject, and the run now says so by name instead of silently. What would let the withheld standing become WideningApplied is Strict preparation of every admitted module within the per-PR runner's memory class and time cap. That is one route to this drop's restoration and not a replacement for its trigger, and applying it also needs the standing population above to be empty or rostered, or every checker change turns red on debt it did not cause."
}
